%N A112899 A skew Pell-Pascal triangle.
%C A112899 Main diagonal is A000129. Row sums are A002605. Column sums are A006190(n+1).
%C A112899 A skewed version of the Riordan array (1/(1-2x-x^2), x/(1-2x-x^2)), see A054456. - _Philippe Deléham_, Nov 21 2007
%C A112899 Triangle, read by rows, given by [0,1/2,-1/2,0,0,0,0,0,...] DELTA [2,1/2,-1/2,0,0,0,0,0,...] where DELTA is the operator defined in A084938. - _Philippe Deléham_, Jan 30 2010
%H A112899 Mark Norfleet, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/43-2/paper43-2-12.pdf">Characterization of second-order strong divisibility sequences of polynomials</a>, The Fibonacci Quarterly, 43(2) (2005), 166-169.
%F A112899 G.f.: 1/(1-2*x*y*(1+x/2)-x^2*y^2).
%F A112899 T(n, k) = Sum_{j=0..floor((2*k-n)/2)} C(k-j, n-k)*C(2*k-n-j, j)*2^(2*k-2*j-n). [corrected by _Jason Yuen_, Jan 21 2025]
%F A112899 T(n, k) = 2*T(n-1, k-1) + T(n-2, k-1) + T(n-2, k-2).
%F A112899 From _Peter Bala_, Nov 09 2026: (Start)
%F A112899 The following assumes that the row indexing starts at n = 1.
%F A112899 Recurrence for row polynomials: R(n, y) = 2*y*R(n-1, y) + y*(1 + y)*R(n-2, y) with R(1, y) = 1 and R(2, y) = 2*y.
%F A112899 The sequence of row polynomials [1, 2*y, y + 5*y^2, 4*y^2 + 12*y^3, ...] is a strong divisibility sequence of polynomials in the ring Z[y] (apply Norfleet, Theorem 3).
%F A112899 R(n, y) = Pell(n) * y^floor(n/2) * Product_{k = 1..floor((n-1)/2)} ( y + cos(k*Pi/n)^2/(1 + cos(k*Pi/n)^2) ).
%F A112899 R(n, -1) = (-1)^(n+1) * 2^(n-1); R(n, 2) = A085939(n); R(n, -2) = (-1)^(n+1) * A090017(n); R(n,-3) = (-1)^(n+1) * A057089(n-1). (End)
%e A112899 Rows begin:
%e A112899   1;
%e A112899   0,   2;
%e A112899   0,   1,   5;
%e A112899   0,   0,   4,  12;
%e A112899   0,   0,   1,  14,  29;
